    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>

    <p><strong>Application:</strong> Regional Voice AI</p>
    <p><strong>Developer:</strong> SHAMEEM KM</p>
    <p><strong>Effective date:</strong> October 12, 2026</p>

    <h2>1. Introduction</h2>

    <p>
        Welcome to Regional Voice AI. Your privacy is important to us.
        This Privacy Policy explains how information may be collected,
        processed, used, stored, and shared when you use our application.
    </p>

    <p>
        Regional Voice AI provides AI-powered conversations, voice
        interaction, text input, speech recognition, text-to-speech,
        and regional language and dialect features.
    </p>

    <h2>2. Information We May Process</h2>

    <p>Depending on the features you use and how the application is implemented,
    the following information may be processed:</p>

    <ul>
        <li>
            <strong>Text and conversations:</strong>
            Questions, messages, AI responses, and conversation history.
        </li>

        <li>
            <strong>Voice information:</strong>
            Audio captured when you use voice input, along with speech
            recognition results or transcripts.
        </li>

        <li>
            <strong>Language preferences:</strong>
            Your selected language, regional dialect, accent preferences,
            and other personalization settings.
        </li>

        <li>
            <strong>Technical information:</strong>
            Information necessary to operate the application, diagnose
            errors, maintain security, and improve reliability.
        </li>

        <li>
            <strong>Location information:</strong>
            Location information only if a location-related feature
            requests or otherwise processes it.
        </li>
    </ul>

    <p>
        The information actually collected depends on the features enabled
        in the released version of the application.
    </p>

    <h2>3. Microphone and Voice Processing</h2>

    <p>
        Regional Voice AI may request microphone permission when you choose
        to interact with the application using your voice.
    </p>

    <p>
        Audio may be processed to recognize speech, generate an AI response,
        and provide spoken output. Depending on the speech recognition and
        AI services used, audio or transcripts may be transmitted to
        external service providers for processing.
    </p>

    <p>
        Microphone access should be used only for the features that require
        it. Whether audio is temporarily processed, stored, or retained
        depends on the application's implementation and the services used.
    </p>

    <h2>4. How We Use Information</h2>

    <p>Information may be used for the following purposes:</p>

    <ul>
        <li>To answer questions and generate AI responses.</li>
        <li>To provide voice input and spoken responses.</li>
        <li>To support regional languages, dialects, and slang.</li>
        <li>To maintain conversation history when this feature is enabled.</li>
        <li>To remember preferences when a supported personalization
            feature is enabled.</li>
        <li>To maintain application security and troubleshoot errors.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>5. AI and Third-Party Services</h2>

    <p>
        Some features may rely on third-party AI models, speech recognition
        services, text-to-speech providers, hosting services, or other
        technical service providers.
    </p>

    <p>
        When such services are used, information necessary to provide the
        requested feature may be sent to those providers and processed
        according to their applicable terms and privacy policies.
    </p>

    <p>
        Third-party providers may have their own data retention and
        processing practices. Users should review the applicable policies
        of the providers actually integrated into the application.
    </p>

    <h2>6. Data Storage and Retention</h2>

    <p>
        Conversation history, preferences, and other information may be
        stored locally on your device or on external servers, depending
        on the features and storage systems used by the application.
    </p>

    <p>
        Information is retained only according to the application's actual
        storage configuration and applicable service-provider policies.
        Before publishing this policy, the developer must specify where
        conversations and preferences are stored, how long they are kept,
        and how users can delete them.
    </p>

    <h2>7. Data Sharing</h2>

    <p>
        Information may be shared with service providers when necessary
        to operate AI conversations, voice processing, hosting, or other
        features you request.
    </p>

    <p>
        The application should not share personal information for purposes
        unrelated to its disclosed functionality without an appropriate
        legal basis or consent where required.
    </p>

    <h2>8. Data Security</h2>

    <p>
        Reasonable technical and organizational measures should be used
        to protect information handled by the application. However,
        no method of electronic storage or internet transmission can
        be guaranteed to be completely secure.
    </p>

    <h2>9. Your Choices and Data Deletion</h2>

    <p>
        You can control permissions through your Android device settings.
        You may also be able to clear locally stored application data
        through Android settings.
    </p>

    <p>
        Clearing application data on your device may not delete information
        already stored on external servers or by third-party providers.
        Any server-side deletion process must be described and made
        available according to the application's actual capabilities.
    </p>

    <h2>10. Children's Privacy</h2>

    <p>
        The application is not intended to collect children's personal
        information in violation of applicable privacy laws.
        If you believe a child has provided personal information in a way
        that violates applicable requirements, contact the developer.
    </p>

    <h2>11. Changes to This Policy</h2>

    <p>
        This Privacy Policy may be updated when application features,
        data practices, or legal requirements change. The updated policy
        will be published on this page with a revised effective date.
    </p>

